% c104: 319 Hn 2 F sharp 4 on beat 1 (was B3), as 119: no major second inside the horns (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 102-103); c082 kept (no D sharp under the tail E).
% c082: 319 Hn 2 B3 on beat 1, Tpt 2 motive x on F sharp 4 (no D sharp under the tail E, A-S PDF 474 Ex. 27-16a); 316 Hn 1 F sharp 4 on beat 1 (no B4 under the flat-9 C5, A-S PDF 469-470).
% c085: 305 Vla "non div." as at 105. 306 Vln II: no down-bow sign (the stroke falls down-bow anyway, as in Vln I and at 106; Adler PDF 38: mark bowings only against habit).
% THEME A, ff tutti, bars 305-320 (= 105-120), then the close 321-324 (= 133-134, 137-138), leading on V into the coda.
% c023: close cut from 8 to 4 bars: the dying motive x no longer stops on E pp with an empty bar and then restarts at the same pitch
%   in the same cellos at the coda; the cellos' V (now 324) leads straight into the coda's i (now 325) (A&S PDF 585: rhythm, texture and dynamics shape a join; c113: c023 gave the v23 numbers 328/329).
% c022: 315 viola B+A, Hn 1 B, Hn 2 F sharp (as sC 111).

% c024: Fl 1 takes the upper octave in 309-312 and 317-320 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 118: a recurring tutti is rescored by extending its range; Ex. 205-206), so the reprise tutti is not a copy of 105-120
% c052/c092: 305 the soprano seventh A5 of the V7 at 304 resolves by step in its own register: Cl 1 G5 on beat 1 (see sC.ily)
%   (A-S PDF 406-407 sec. 9, Ex. 24-11: a transferred resolution needs the tone of resolution in the same register).
% c124: 305-308 the flutes rest and enter a2 at 309 in the octave above the violins (were a2 at pitch with Vln I, Vln II/Ob 1 on E5-B5 and B4, the flute's
%   weak low-middle register under ff brass: Adler I PDF 185). Adler II PDF 151 (Mozart 40/iv: every instrument placed where every note tells), PDF 152 (Beethoven 9/i:
%   the high flute octave carries alone), PDF 150 (Barber: the doubling grows with each statement), PDF 156 (a rest before a colour makes its entry heard).
%   The top octave cannot start at 305 (B6 at 307 is kept for the coda peak), so the first phrase is strings, oboe, clarinets and cor anglais. Cl 1 G5 still resolves the seventh (c092).
dCFluteOne = { R2.*4 | e'''4-.\ff b''8-. b''-. e'''4-. | a'''2->( gis'''8 g'''8 | fis'''4-.) dis'''8-. dis'''-. b''4-. | e'''4-\sysLabel "a2"-. r4 r4 | a''4-. g''-. fis''-. | e''4-. dis''8-. dis''-. e''4-. | fis''4-.( g''8 a''8) b''4-. | c'''2->( b''8 fis''8) | e'''4-. b''8-. b''-. e'''4-. | g'''2->( fis'''8 f'''8 | e'''4-.) dis'''8-. dis'''-. fis'''4-. | e'''4-. r4 r4 | R2.*4 | }
dCFluteTwo = { R2.*4 | e'''4-.\ff b''8-. b''-. e'''4-. | a'''2->( gis'''8 g'''8 | fis'''4-.) dis'''8-. dis'''-. b''4-. | e'''4-. r4 r4 | a''4-. g''-. fis''-. | e''4-. dis''8-. dis''-. e''4-. | fis''4-.( g''8 a''8) b''4-. | c'''2->( b''8 fis''8) | e'''4-. b''8-. b''-. e'''4-. | g'''2->( fis'''8 f'''8 | e'''4-.) dis'''8-. dis'''-. fis'''4-. | e'''4-. r4 r4 | R2.*4 | }  % c078: 109-112 and 117-120 Fl 2 joins Fl 1 in the upper octave (was the lower octave B4-A5 at ff, the flute's weak register under the tutti; Adler PDF 185)
dCOboeOne = { \partCombineApart e''4-. b'8-. b'-. e''4-. | \partCombineSoloI g''2->( fis''8 f''8 | e''4-.) b''8-. b''-. g''4-. | fis''4-. dis''-. b'-. | e''4-. b'8-. b'-. e''4-. | a''2->( gis''8 g''8 | fis''4-.) dis''8-. dis''-. b'4-. | e''4-\sysLabel "1."-. r4 r4 | a''4-. g''-. fis''-. | e''4-. dis''8-. dis''-. e''4-. | fis''4-.( g''8 a''8) b''4-. | c'''2->( b''8 fis''8) | e''4-. b'8-. b'-. e''4-. | g''2->( fis''8 f''8 | e''4-.) dis''8-. dis''-. fis''4-. | e''4-. r4 r4 | \partCombineAutomatic R2. | R2.*3 | }
