% c086: Bsn 1 breathes at 316 with Hn 4 (dCHnFour), as at 116.
% c189: 317 tenor countermelody (Bsn 1, Hn 3, Vc) G3 then E4, as 117.
% c358: 105/305 "espress." on Bsn 1 and Hn 3(-4), which double the cellos' countermelody (marked espress.) at the same ff (Sebesky Ex. 281, PDF 214-215). No accent or dynamic added (soft-brass rule).
dCBsnOne = { g2.(^\markup \italic "espress." | b2 e'4~ | e'2 b4 | a2 fis4 | g2.) | a2( c'4~ | c'4 b4 a4 | g2.) | c'2.( | b2. | a2 c'4 | b2 a4) \breathe | g2( e'4~ | e'2 g4 | a2 fis4 | g4) r4 r4 | e2.--(\p | e2.-- | e2.--)\> | R2.\! | }
% c014: 309-324 the sustained bass goes to Bsn 2 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 101, 104); c159: the trombones and tuba rest through dC since c034, so the old note about the bass trombone doubling the tuba no longer applies; Tpt 2 E4 (not D sharp) in the tonic bar 313
% c362 (A&S Unit 5, PDF 83): Bsn 2 stops on beat 3 of 309 and 317, where the tune's E (beat 3) leaps to the next root with the bass (E-A, E-G): no octaves E-A/E-G with the tune, as at 312 (c066)
dCBsnTwo = { e,2. | e,2. | e,2. | b,2. | e,2 r4 | a,2. | b,2. | e,2 r4 | fis,2. | g,2. | a,2. | b,2. | e,2 r4 | g,2. | b,2. | e,4 r4 r4 | R2.*4 | }  % c066: breath for Bsn 2 at the theme's phrase end (Vln I rests on beats 2-3 here): 24 bars of ff sustained bass otherwise (Adler PDF 230, 292)
% c148: 305-320 (as 105-120 in sC) Cb and Cbsn tenuto, not accent, on every tutti downbeat, as the tuba, bass trombone and timpani (c124, c146): the bar line already carries the metrical accent in one-to-the-bar 3/4, and 16 equal accents flatten the four-bar hypermeasure (Aldwell-Schachter Unit 3 PDF 50, 53); Dvorak 9/iii marks accents only where they go against the metre.
dCCbsn = { e,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | b,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | a,,4-- r4 r4 | b,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | fis,,4-- r4 r4 | g,,4-- r4 r4 | a,,4-- r4 r4 | b,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | g,,4-- r4 r4 | b,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | R2.*4 | }
% c124: 305-320 the brass downbeat crotchets tenuto instead of accented (horns ff, low brass f unchanged): Dan's listening rule (BRIEF: brass weight, not bite);
%   Adler II PDF 147-148 (d'Indy: trombones held under the tutti so they do not dominate), PDF 154 (Smetana: the brass give the fast tutti roundness, not edge).
% c165: Hn 1-4 do not restate ff at 305: the ff reached at 304 stands (one dynamic per change, MOLA PDF 8 and Ex. 3)
% c189: 313 beat 3 Hn 1 A4 (was C5), as 113.
% c202: 310 Hn 1 beat 3 A4 (was C5): C5-B4 against the tune's G-F# into 311 made the IV8-7-V parallel fifths of Aldwell-Schachter Ex. 12-21 (PDF 190) between Hn 1 and the melody; A4 steps to B4 as at 113/313 (c189)
% c272: 310 Hn 1 rests on beat 3, as 110 (sC.ily)
dCHnOne = { b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 r4 | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | c''4-- r4 r4 | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | c''4-- r4 a'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | c''4-- r4 c''4-. | fis'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 r4 | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | R2.*4 | }  % c011: no E on beat 3 of 106/118 (310/322) under the chromatic tail F sharp-F-E (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 54) % c066: Hn 1 on B4/C5 (written F#5/G5), not E5 (written B5, a semitone under the professional ceiling C6 in Adler App. A, adler2 PDF 305); Hn 3 takes the middle G4/A4/F#4 (Adler PDF 303-304: III between I and II); Hn 3 beat 1 only at 106/118 (G against the tail F#-F)
dCHnTwo = { e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 r4 | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | dis'4-- r4 dis'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | dis'4-- r4 dis'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | dis'4-- r4 dis'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 r4 | fis'4-- r4 dis'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | R2.*4 | }  % c046: Hn 2 takes the E4 crotchets and Hn 3 the B4 (Adler PDF 303: I and III high, II and IV low)
% c114: 305-320 Hn 4 leaves the tenor countermelody (Hn 3, Bsn 1, Vc keep it) and holds the bass an octave above Bsn 2 (E3, B2, A2, F#3, G3): with the low brass
%   held back in the reprise, the downbeats had nothing between the bass and the tenor (E2-E4 at 307/317, F#2-C4 at 313, G2-E4 at 318); every full tutti chord
%   in Rimsky-Korsakov's appendix (PDF 505-507) fills the octave above the bass, and PDF 125: outer parts are seldom separated without the intermediate octaves.
% c226: Hn 4's ff low line 305-312 split at 309/310 with a breath, as Hn 3 phrases it (5+3 bars) and as at 105-112; it was eight ff bars in the low register on one slur, 5.2 s on one breath (Adler PDF 292, 303, 309).
% c362 (A&S Unit 5, PDF 76, 83, 86): G3 at 305, 307, 312, 317: the third on 307's downbeat (was a bare E-B fifth in the tutti), and no octaves with the tune F#-E (304-305), B-E (311-312), E-G (317-318); rests on beat 3 of 308-309 (the breath moves there from 309/310), so the held B and E no longer meet the tune's beat-3 B/E and move with it; Bsn 2 keeps the octave above the bass
dCHnFour = { g2.( | e2. | g2. | b,2) r4 | e2 r4 | a,2.( | b,2. | g2) r4 | fis2.( | g2. | a,2. | b,2.) \once \override BreathingSign.direction = #DOWN \breathe | g2.( | g2. | b,2. | e4) r4 r4 | R2.*4 | }  % c115: treble again after 301-320 in bass clef (see dB.ily); c155: that clef now stands before the entry at 331 (coda.ily). c046: the 16-bar forte legato is split at 116/117 (316/317) for a breath (Adler PDF 292, 309: a slur is one breath)
% c025: Hn 3 and Hn 4 exchanged at 105-120/305-320: the low countermelody (G3-E4) was in Hn 3, the upper voice of the shared staff, under Hn 4's E4 crotchets, so the voices crossed in every bar (Gould, Behind Bars PDF 41, 50-51)
% c097: 305-320 Hn 3 joins Hn 4 in unison on the tenor countermelody (with Vc and Bsn 1); Hn 1-2 keep the crotchet chords on beats 1 and 3
%   (Adler II PDF 44: two horns in unison equal one trumpet or trombone; one horn under three ff horns, trumpets and four low brass is covered).
% c358: 105/305 "espress." on Bsn 1 and Hn 3(-4), which double the cellos' countermelody (marked espress.) at the same ff (Sebesky Ex. 281, PDF 214-215). No accent or dynamic added (soft-brass rule).
dCHnThree = { g2.(^\markup \italic "espress." | b2 e'4~ | e'2 b4 | a2 fis4 | g2.) | a2( c'4~ | c'4 b4 a4 | g2.) | c'2.( | b2. | a2 c'4 | b2 a4) \breathe | g2( e'4~ | e'2 g4 | a2 fis4 | g4) r4 r4 | R2.*4 | }  % c024: 4 surplus rest bars removed (Hn 4 ran 4 bars late from 321 to past the final bar). c011: no E on beat 3 of 106/118 (310/322) under the chromatic tail F sharp-F-E (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 54)
