% c029: 305-320 Vln II takes theme A an octave lower (with Cl 2 and the cor anglais), so the reprise tutti is not a copy of 105-120:
%   strings in octaves and the range extended at both ends (Fl 1 above since c024). Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 117-118: an idea is scored differently
%   each time it recurs, by transfer into other octaves and extension of range (Ex. 178-181, 192-195, 205-206).
% c159: 305-308 Vln II plays the head in unison with Vln I as at 105-108 (Adler PDF 152, 255, 268): with the flutes resting until 309 and ff horns and trumpets underneath, Vln I and Ob 1 alone could not carry it; the lower octave (c029) now starts at 309, four bars earlier than 113
