% c287: 106, 110, 118 (306, 310, 318 in dC) the violas' beat-3 off-beat no longer strikes the tail's starting note (G4, A4) a semitone or tone above the tail's lower octave F sharp 4-F4 / G sharp 4-G4 (C.a., Cl 2; Vln II too at 118/318): beat 3 is B3 at 106/118 and C4-E4 at 110. Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 76: in a string-wind combination of equal power the strings predominate, so the bowed staccato chord covered the two winds' chromatic descent in that octave; PDF 78: of two octaves it is the lower one that needs support. As c011 removed the horns' E and G on these beats.
% c353: 314 violas B3/E4 on beats 2-3 (were B3/G4), as at 114: over the passing bass G the tutti's neighbour D sharp made G-B-D sharp, a root-position augmented III,
%   on beat 2 at ff (Aldwell-Schachter PDF 240, Points for Review 7, PDF 245: avoid III with raised 7 in minor; apparent augmented triads should be 6/3 chords of dominant function). With E4 held the beat is i6 with the melody's lower neighbour, as at 114.
